#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of intel-media"
msgstr "Instalação do intel-media"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/multimedia/libdriv/intel-media.xml:131
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This package takes a long time to build because it compiles code specific to"
" each individual generation of Intel GPUs and for a variety of media codecs."
msgstr ""
"Esse pacote leva muito tempo para construir porque compila código específico"
" para cada geração individual de GPUs da Intel e para uma variedade de "
"codificadores de mídia."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/multimedia/libdriv/intel-media.xml:143
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you know the model of your Intel GPU, you can pass the "
"<option>-D{GEN{8,9,11,12},MTL,ARL}=OFF</option> option to the "
"<command>cmake</command> command but leaving the option for your GPU out.  "
"Note that the <quote>GEN</quote> number here is the generation of the GPU, "
"not the CPU.  For example, with an Intel Core i7-1065G7 CPU shipping a 11th-"
"generation Intel GPU, the <option>-D{GEN{8,9,12},MTL,ARL}=OFF</option> "
"option can be used so the code specific to the other generations of Intel "
"GPUs won't be built."
msgstr ""
"Se conhecer o modelo da tua GPU Intel, você pode passar a opção "
"<option>-D{GEN{8,9,11,12},MTL,ARL}=OFF</option> para o comando "
"<command>cmake</command>, mas deixando a opção para tua GPU de fora. Observe "
"que o número <quote>GEN</quote> aqui é a geração da GPU, não da CPU. Por "
"exemplo, com uma CPU Intel Core i7-1065G7 que envia uma GPU Intel de 11ª "
"geração, a opção <option>-D{GEN{8,9,12},MTL,ARL}=OFF</option> pode ser "
"usada, de forma que o código específico para as outras gerações de GPUs "
"Intel não seria construído."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/multimedia/libdriv/intel-media.xml:155
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To determine the model of the Intel GPU, install <xref linkend='pciutils'/> "
"and run <command>lspci -nn | grep -Ei 'VGA|DISPLAY'</command> first.  It "
"will output some information about the GPU.  If the output contains "
"<literal>Meteor Lake</literal>, the GPU model is <literal>MTL</literal>.  "
"Otherwise, follow <ulink url='https://dgpu-docs.intel.com/devices/hardware-"
"table.html'/> to find the entry for your GPU and the model of the GPU should"
" be in the <quote>Architecture</quote> column.  The Xe and XeHPG "
"architectures are covered by the <literal>GEN12</literal> model."
msgstr ""
"Para determinar o modelo da GPU Intel, instale <xref linkend='pciutils'/> e "
"execute <command>lspci -nn | grep -Ei 'VGA|DISPLAY'</command> primeiro. Ele "
"produzirá algumas informações acerca da GPU. Se a saída gerada contiver "
"<literal>Meteor Lake</literal>, o modelo da GPU será <literal>MTL</literal>. "
"Caso contrário, siga <ulink url='https://dgpu-docs.intel.com/devices/"
"hardware-table.html'/> para encontrar a entrada para tua GPU e o modelo da "
"GPU deveria estar na coluna <quote>Architecture</quote>. As arquiteturas Xe "
"e XeHPG são cobertas pelo modelo <literal>GEN12</literal>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/multimedia/libdriv/intel-media.xml:181
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>intel-media</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o <application>intel-media</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/multimedia/libdriv/intel-media.xml:185
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$XORG_PREFIX \\\n"
"      -DINSTALL_DRIVER_SYSCONF=OFF        \\\n"
"      -DBUILD_TYPE=Release                \\\n"
"      -G Ninja                            \\\n"
"      -Wno-dev ..                   &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$XORG_PREFIX \\\n"
"      -DINSTALL_DRIVER_SYSCONF=OFF        \\\n"
"      -DBUILD_TYPE=Release                \\\n"
"      -G Ninja                            \\\n"
"      -Wno-dev ..                   &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

